<p>Hungary has signaled it may block the European Union’s planned loan package for Ukraine, tying its approval to the restart of Russian oil deliveries to Hungary via the Druzhba pipeline, which runs through Ukraine. The Hungarian government says oil transit stopped in late January and argues Ukraine is using energy supplies as leverage — a claim Kyiv rejects, pointing instead to damage from Russian strikes. The standoff complicates the EU’s push to secure new financing for Ukraine, as Brussels looks for unity ahead of the anniversary of Russia’s full-scale invasion.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/zcYyiMQM_LNthTGGAvnxmWsyR0lrR2nTw487Yp3OjoXPv_5wjO7YPFc15QHIOT-tJMBhI_F8GI96GHIzkhzp32Uhpwx77ygUbi26FoxDasSvKmJROzYkMY59tGoDN-BVFD2WyIXMOeunQNG5hXoIpxtlHozqgq97yJ3IXFOKYEH3z5bf82nEkrXQUlYsYh3v4OEOepO-Hw76Uk3Mm10SFP2p' alt='The Hungarian foreign minister, Peter Szijjarto, in Prague, Czech Republic, last month.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Unanimity needed: The loan requires unanimous approval from all 27 EU member states, giving Hungary a clear veto over the entire package.</li><li>Cash pressure: POLITICO reports Ukraine’s funds could start running low from April, raising the pressure on Brussels to bridge the financing and energy-transit dispute.</li><li>Election backdrop: Several outlets say Prime Minister Viktor Orbán has sharpened his anti-Ukraine rhetoric ahead of an election in which he risks losing power after more than 15 years.</li></ul><blockquote>We will not give in to this blackmail. - Péter Szijjártó</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Hungarian government: Foreign Minister Péter Szijjártó said Hungary is blocking the loan until Druzhba oil transit resumes, and accused Ukraine of “blackmail.” (<a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/hungary-delays-eus-e90b-loan-to-ukraine/'>POLITICO Europe</a>)</li><li>Ukraine: Ukraine rejects Hungary’s claim that it halted energy transit for political reasons, and says Russian strikes damaged energy infrastructure, according to POLITICO’s account of Kyiv’s position. (<a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/hungary-delays-eus-e90b-loan-to-ukraine/'>POLITICO Europe</a>)</li><li>European Commission: The Commission convened an emergency meeting to address the Druzhba disruption, POLITICO reports. (<a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/hungary-delays-eus-e90b-loan-to-ukraine/'>POLITICO Europe</a>)</li><li>New York Times analysis: The New York Times says the delay may end up being procedural, even as Hungary signals it could still create headaches for the EU’s plan. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/20/world/europe/euro-loan-ukraine-hungary-obstacle.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/hungary-threatens-veto-of-€90-billion-eu-loan-to-ukraine/a-76067806'>Hungary threatens veto of €90 billion EU loan to Ukraine</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/hungary-threatens-to-block-ukraine-aid-over-oil-row'>Hungary threatens to block Ukraine aid over oil row</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/2/20/hungary-to-block-90-billion-euro-eu-loan-to-ukraine-in-russian-oil-dispute'>Hungary to block 90 billion euro EU loan to Ukraine in Russian oil dispute</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/20/world/europe/euro-loan-ukraine-hungary-obstacle.html'>Hungary Poses Unexpected Hurdle to Europe’s 90-Billion Euro Loan to Ukraine</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/9bb03b35-2bf5-44fb-b02e-0dbbc3b87b7f'>Hungary blocks €90bn EU loan to Ukraine days before war anniversary</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/hungary-delays-eus-e90b-loan-to-ukraine/'>EU’s €90B plan to fund Ukraine in jeopardy as Hungary blocks deal</a> - politico.eu</li><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/news/632847-hungary-block-eu-loan-ukraine/'>Hungary blocks EU loan to Ukraine</a> - rt.com</li></ul>